\label{maintheorem}
If $G$ is a graph and $H$ is a rigid $d$-cube in $G$ with $H$ monophobic in $G$, then
\begin{enumerate}
\item 
If $\gamma \in C_d(G)$ is a homology cycle containing exactly one nonzero term supported by $H$, then $[\gamma]\ne [0]$ in $H_d(G)$.
\item If $\alpha: (I_\infty^d, \partial I_\infty^d) \to (G,v_0)$ is a based graph map in which small cubes supported by $H$ appear an odd number of times, then
$[\alpha] \ne [0]$ in $A_d(G,v_0)$.
\end{enumerate}

