\label{k23lemma}
For the neighborhoods $K^{\{d\}}$ and $K_{23}^{\{d\}}$ defined above, we have:
\begin{enumerate}
\item
$K^{\{d\}}$ is monotolerant for $d=1,2$ but monophobic for $d\ge 3$.
\item
$K_{23}^{\{d\}}$ is monotolerant for all $d\ge 2$.
\end{enumerate}

Monotolerance of $K^{\{1\}}$ and $K^{\{2\}}\approx K_{23}^{\{2\}}$ has been noted earlier. 
We will first demonstrate that $K^{\{3\}}$ is monophobic, by an argument that generalizes easily to dimensions $d>3$. Suppose
we have a 4-cube $\sigma$ which is monotolerant witness for $K^{\{3\}}$, with bottom face (following $H$) labeled as shown:
